Subject: [PATCH 1/3] SFS v170: sports Quick Play Guide + 2-mode house rules +
 edition wording

Sports vaults now open an animated Quick Play Guide before launch, replacing
the terse .rules line for sports only (music/film keep the old copy untouched).

- Quick Play Guide (sports-gated on v.sp): CORRECT first / PASS second, phone
  acts out the tilt on a 5.6s CSS-3D loop with the rings, pills and flanking
  arrows lighting in sync. Down-arrow is green to match the in-game correct
  flash. Honours prefers-reduced-motion.
- tryFree() branches: sports -> guide, everything else runs the original body
  (renamed qpgLaunch) byte-identical. Mode selection rides the existing &clue=
  param; dropped the !V5SPORT guard so sports passes it too.
- House rules folded 3 -> 2 modes: Beginner "Hum it, sing it, or say it.
  Anything goes." / Superfan "Lyrics only, no chorus." Casual removed
  everywhere in this file; V5CLUE resets per vault so nobody is stranded.
- Edition wording aligned to the film pattern for music and sports: dare line
  + "Choose Your Edition". Sports uses "deep bench" (native sports idiom) in
  both the dare line and the Deluxe description; music keeps "deep cuts".
  Dropped the now-redundant "Both editions included" note.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012avjdYG8yRCMZ3uJswRWwC
