From: Rose <accounting@hutch-design.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 14:08:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] SFS v171: Quick Play Guide becomes the sports opening
 screen in play.html
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The guide moved out of index.html and into play.html, replacing the sStart
copy for sports vaults. Reason: the guide's TAP TO PLAY has to BE the gesture
gate — goFullscreen / buzz / unlockAudio / requestPerm all need a user gesture
in the document that asks, and gesture context does not survive the navigation
from index.html to play.html. Running it on index.html would have left the
player tapping "tap to play" twice and re-reading the tilt rules they were
just taught.

- renderQPG() replaces #sStart's contents when ED==='sports'; music and film
  keep the existing start screen untouched.
- Its CTA fires the identical bundle the old startBtn did, then ready().
- Accent auto-derives from the team's own card outline via spCard(), with a
  luminance guard so a near-white outline falls back to the card background.
  Chrome stays dark on every team — light primaries (Steelers gold, Spurs
  silver) would break white text if used as a background.
- Mode picker sets RCLUE in-page and pre-selects from the &clue= param.
- play.html's own house-rules row folded 3 -> 2 to match index.html; Casual
  removed and the Beginner copy synced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012avjdYG8yRCMZ3uJswRWwC
