MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sportcard class was only applied at show('sGame'), so the forehead screen
and the 3-2-1 were still rendering on the default purple. Team card colours are
now applied at boot for sports, before the first screen paints.

- applySportCard() sets --cardbg / --cardoutline / --olw and adds .sportcard
  once, up front; the existing per-round call now reuses it.
- White fill + team-outline lettering (the same -webkit-text-stroke technique
  as the game card) applied to .fhText, #getReady, #big, #score and .wallHead,
  with per-element stroke widths so the small text doesn't clog.
- Unlock wall: "That's the taste" and the buy button take the team outline;
  the mix phrase is now a swappable span — sports reads "players, coaches,
  stadiums & team lore" instead of the music-only "songs, lyrics & lore".
- Fix: #sStart.qpgmode declared display at id+class specificity, which beat
  .screen{display:none} and left the guide painted behind every later screen.
  Display is now scoped to .on.

